  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shahzad @ Bablu @ Baddu vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 28 October, 2021 Author: Arun Kumar Sharma Bench: Arun Kumar Sharma 1 Mcrc-41451-2021 The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh Mcrc-41451-2021 (Shahzad @ Bablu @ Baddu Vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh)",
    "facts": "This is the first application filed by the applicant under Section 439 of the Cr.P.C. seeking regular bail. The applicant is in custody since 31.05.2021 in connection with Crime No.447/2021 registered at Police Station Cant., District Sagar for the offence punishable under Sections 34(2), 49A of the Excise Act and under Sections 50, 1, 54, 56, 59 & 63 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006. As per the case of the prosecution, about 50 liters of country made liquor along with other articles have been seized from the joint possession of the applicant and other accused persons, which was unfit for human consumption. Investigation is complete and charge sheet has been filed. The applicant is the first offender. Learned Panel Lawyer for the State has opposed the application, however, he has submitted that the chemical analysis report of the liquor is still awaited.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant submits that the applicant is innocent, he has been falsely implicated in the case.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant submits that the applicant is innocent, he has been falsely implicated in the case.",
